   {
    "code": "occupancy_not_stored",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Of 66439 occupancy entries MetaMorpheus wrote, some are not in ptm_stoichiometry: 10131 site not in ptm_sites. 'site not in ptm_sites' means the entry's site has no ptm_sites row to key on; 'not determinable' means a cell's segments could not be assigned to its accessions from the sequences (QuantProject DEF-OCC-ACCESSION), which is never guessed. Absence of a row for these sites is therefore not NA. A 'duplicate' is a second entry for a (site, run) that already has a row: one with identical values loses nothing; one with DIFFERENT values means MetaMorpheus wrote two answers and the first in file order was stored (examples in bundle.json occupancy.differing_duplicates; which one should be stored is QuantProject's to define)."
   },
   {
    "code": "peptide_rows_localization_ambiguous",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "38 row(s) of AllQuantifiedPeptides.tsv name several full sequences, joined by `|`: a peptide whose modification site the search did not settle (MetaMorpheus #2917). Their 211 value(s) are not stored, since storing them under one of the sequences would place them on a site the search never decided. The PSMs behind them are in `psms`. E.g. `AAQPPTETAESS[UniProt:Phosphoserine on S]QAEEEKDAVDEAKPK|AAQPPTETAES[UniProt:Phosphoserine on S]SQAEEEKDAVDEAKPK`, `AEAAAAPAPAAGP[Common Biological:Hydroxylation on P]GQMSFTFASPTQVFFDSANVK|AEAAAAPAP[Common Biological:Hydroxylation on P]AAGPGQMSFTFASPTQVFFDSANVK|AEAAAAP[Common Biological:Hydroxylation on P]APAAGPGQMSFTFASPTQVFFDSANVK`, `AELAPETTETPVET[UniProt:Phosphothreonine on T]PETVQATDLSLNPEEGSK|AELAPETTET[UniProt:Phosphothreonine on T]PVETPETVQATDLSLNPEEGSK`."
   },
   {
    "code": "sdrf_partial",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "The SDRF was used only for the runs it names that were searched: it names no row for 2 searched run(s), each given a synthetic sample with no annotation: Eclipse_02855_MmBrain_FP_NBF_LFQ_C132_1_2, Eclipse_02868_MmBrain_FP_NBF_LFQ_C83_2_4. sdrf_status is `partial`."
   },
   {
    "code": "sdrf_uncoded",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "The deposited SDRF describes its samples only as text with no ontology term, so the curated organism part, cell type, disease and individual columns are empty. The text is in sample_characteristics: organism part: Frontal lobe. Match on it as text; it has not been mapped to a term."
   },
   {
    "code": "unplaced_ptm_sites",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Some modifications on peptides shared between proteins were not written to ptm_sites for one or more of those proteins, because the peptide could not be located in that protein's sequence and the producer's residue spans cannot be paired with its accessions. Of the (PSM, protein) pairs affected: 973 named a protein that does not contain the stored peptide -- typically a PSM ambiguous between peptide sequences (level 4 or 5), where this protein carries a different candidate than the first, which is the one stored. Sites on the other proteins of the same PSMs are written. Counts are in bundle.json under protein_databases."
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_decoy_groups",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "343 occupancy entries on decoy protein groups were not stored: MetaMorpheus computes them, and they are FDR machinery, not biology."
   }
  ],
